  "findings": [
    "All six navigations read all 57 resources from cache with transferSize 0; the document itself responded within 9–26 ms.",
    "Disabling Fetch did not consistently remove the delay: local display remained 1324.5–2535.0 ms and exceeded 500 ms on all three diagnostic runs.",
    "The main module first-execution to initial render-return interval consumed 731.3–1226.0 ms across six runs and aligned with a 733–1229 ms long task. This is a directly observed main-thread initialization/render cost, not an external I/O wait.",
    "The delay before initial main execution varied widely even with Fetch disabled. This experiment does not attribute that gap to an exact browser, parser, instrumentation, or application task.",
    "Additional long tasks occurred after initial local display. Long-task sums cover the diagnostic collection interval and must not be interpreted as time before local display.",
    "Three diagnostic samples do not replace the 20-sample before/after benchmark or establish a production p95. Actual NEXUS host app switching remains unmeasured."
